      "title": "How it works",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## OneShot MV: app\n\nThis workflow opens as an **app**: the settings on the right, the results in the middle. **App / Graph** at the top left shows the graph behind it.\n\nLoad a song, write a World, turn **Preview only** on and click **Run** to see every shot without rendering anything. Then turn it off and run again. The video lands in `output/oneshot-mv/runs/<run>/final_<format>.mp4`, and the Studio (the OneShot MV button) shows it as it renders.\n\n**Who sings**: Crowd, or Single Artist from a description (**New artist**). For a photo, switch to Graph and un-bypass **Artist photo**. **World images**: a folder of your own images instead of a World line.\n\nEvery other setting is on the Director in the graph; hover any of them for more. Use music you have the rights to."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
